1
00:00:00,379 --> 00:00:03,619
(Sheldon:)Unlike my mole, which is holding
steady at the size of a navy bean.

2
00:00:05,718 --> 00:00:06,718
(Sheldon:)What's next?

3
00:00:06,885 --> 00:00:08,725
(Sheldon:)This is the very copy

4
00:00:08,887 --> 00:00:11,057
(Sheldon:)of The Handbook
of Chemistry and Physics

5
00:00:11,223 --> 00:00:14,573
(Sheldon:)in which I looked up the reaction
rates of mendelevium and....

6
00:00:16,695 --> 00:00:18,075
(Amy:)-And what?
-No.

7
00:00:19,465 --> 00:00:22,075
(Sheldon:)-No, no, no, no.
-What's wrong?

8
00:00:24,503 --> 00:00:26,243
(Sheldon:)I've made a horrible mistake.

9
00:00:26,405 --> 00:00:27,405
(Amy:)What are you talking about?

10
00:00:27,573 --> 00:00:30,553
(Sheldon:)This table,
it's in square centimeters.

11
00:00:30,709 --> 00:00:32,249
I read it as square meters.

12
00:00:32,411 --> 00:00:33,651
(Sheldon:)You know what that means?

13
00:00:33,812 --> 00:00:36,052
(Amy:)That Americans can't handle
the metric system?

14
00:00:38,751 --> 00:00:41,701
(Sheldon:)Amy, I was off by a factor of 10,000.

15
00:00:42,554 --> 00:00:44,394
(Amy:)But the Chinese team
found the element.

16
00:00:44,556 --> 00:00:47,396
(Sheldon:)They shouldn't have.
My calculations were wrong.

17
00:00:47,559 --> 00:00:50,269
(Sheldon:)There must be some resonance between
the elements I didn't know about.

18
00:00:50,429 --> 00:00:52,029
(Amy:)So you just got lucky?

19
00:00:52,197 --> 00:00:55,107
Sheldon Cooper does not get lucky!

20
00:00:56,835 --> 00:01:00,025
(Amy:)You and me both, brother.

